{"availability":"available","full":"elgar328/nacre","name":"nacre","description":"Exact b-rep CAD kernel in pure Rust","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-11T07:27:14Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:03:09Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["b-rep","cad","cad-kernel","computational-geometry","rust","wasm"],"demo":"https://elgar328.github.io/nacre-playground/gallery/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:38.776Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:38.776Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:38.776Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:10.955Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-05T05:50:39.950Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-07T11:14:52.432Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T13:18:38.776Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nacre is an exact b-rep CAD kernel. Every topological decision is exact, and it never fails silently.","Named for nacre, mother-of-pearl, which grows one layer at a time and never rewrites the layers beneath. The kernel treats geometry the same way and, unlike most CAD kernels, its topology too."],"features":["Exact by definition. Dimensions keep the decimals you typed: 1.1 is 11/10, not the nearest binary fraction. A vertex is defined by the surfaces that meet there, and its coordinates are only a cache with a proven error…","No global tolerance. Many CAD kernels treat two points as the same whenever they fall within one global epsilon. Nacre makes every decision from the exact definitions instead. A fast f64 check settles most cases, and…","Named errors, not wrong solids. When an operation cannot be computed correctly, Nacre refuses it and names the reason: the case is outside what the kernel supports, it has no valid result, or it points to a bug in the…","Pure Rust, down to the arithmetic. There are no C dependencies, so the same kernel runs natively and in the browser through WebAssembly."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elgar328/nacre/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"71fb0b9d02ed39837edf3f2568d3b2310d555aae4063d299b0006d95eb7a654c","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:11.038Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:55.174Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Nacre is an exact b-rep CAD kernel. Every topological decision is exact, and it never fails silently.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elgar328/nacre/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"71fb0b9d02ed39837edf3f2568d3b2310d555aae4063d299b0006d95eb7a654c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elgar328/nacre/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:55.174Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T23:03:09Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elgar328/nacre/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:55.175Z","hash":"71fb0b9d02ed39837edf3f2568d3b2310d555aae4063d299b0006d95eb7a654c","originalBytes":4528,"storedBytes":4528,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["kernel","nacre","cad","exact","geometry","milestone","browser","built","every","fornjot","never","one","outside","planes","same","solids","step","surfaces","topology","two","any","application","application.","b-rep","boolean","cache","coordinates","coverage","cylinders","decision","done","down","either","errors","files","general","global","grows","including","instead.","kernel.","kernels","layer","made","makes","most","much","named","nurbs","only","parts","planar","playground","points","quadric","rest","runs","rust","scope","status","tessellation","their","there","they","way","what","where","which","work","wrong","after","against","alongside","anything","anything.","apache-2.0","app","appearance","approximated","approximated.","approximations","arcs","arithmetic.","assemblies","axis","began","behind.","belongs","beneath.","binary","bodies","booleans","bound","braun","bug","build","cannot","carry","case","cases","cavities","cha